    "body": "Review fixes pushed (UMA), head 95005b14:\n\n1. **Terminal output after AttachConsole** - done in `crates/ui/src/win_console.rs`: after a successful attach, each of STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE / STD_ERROR_HANDLE whose `GetStdHandle` is NULL or INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE gets a `CreateFileW(\"CONOUT$\")` handle via `SetStdHandle`; valid handles (redirect, pipe) are left alone. Checked against std's source (`library/std/src/sys/stdio/windows.rs`): `Stderr::write` -> `write` -> `get_handle` calls `GetStdHandle` on every write, so `std::io::stderr` / tracing picks up the new handle.\n2. **Visible start-up failure with no console** - Windows-only: `main` shows a `MessageBoxW` when `run` returns non-zero and no console was attached; a panic hook chained after the previous one does the same with the panic text. One box per process; nothing in the hook can panic; no unwrap/expect.\n3. **No-console log destination** - follow-up #1323 filed (P7, effort:medium, area:ui, source:agent, Refs #1278), named in the PR body and the decision note.\n- Changelog line now reads PR #1287.\n\nVerification: Linux quick gate green, clippy `-D warnings` clean. `win_console.rs` compiles and is clippy-clean for `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` standalone; a full `cargo check --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu -p camcraft-ui` was blocked by flecs_ecs_sys's C build (no mingw gcc here). **It was NOT run on Windows** - a Windows tester please confirm the 4 cases: double-click, terminal, redirect, start-up failure (listed in the PR body).\n\nReady for a re-review.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
