    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 95005b14544e3f03f73eb465054d9cbb1f7de0b6 -->\n**Delta review (M3): one defect found after the maintainer's `merge-ready`. Raising it for the maintainer to decide; labels are left as they are.**\n\n**The earlier items are all addressed:**\n- The CONOUT$ std handles after attach: `crates/ui/src/win_console.rs:69-102`.\n- The visible start-up failure on a non-zero exit: `main.rs:19-22`, `win_console.rs:106-130`.\n- The log-file follow-up is filed as #1323.\n\n**Defect: `win_console.rs:135-144` (`install_panic_hook`).** A panic hook fires at panic time, before `catch_unwind` runs. The app catches panics on purpose at:\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/gpu_init.rs:166` (the GPU probe);\n- `shell.rs:910` and `shell_window.rs:220`;\n- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step.rs:133` (a STEP kernel panic becomes a clean import error);\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs:155`;\n- `crates/kernel/src/truck_impl.rs`.\n\nSo on a double-click, a *handled* panic (for example a bad STEP import) pops a modal \"CamCraft stopped unexpectedly\" box and blocks that thread. It also uses up the once-per-process flag, so a later real failure shows nothing.\n\n**Suggested fix:** drop the hook. On Windows only, wrap `camcraft_ui::run(&args)` in `catch_unwind` in `main`, and show the box only when a panic escapes `run`.\n\n**Local results** (macOS host, merged with main 3d1e84e5):\n- camcraft-ui: check OK, clippy clean, lib 617 passed.\n- `win_console.rs` compiled standalone for `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` (check OK, clippy clean).\n- The full Windows crate check was not possible (the flecs C build needs mingw), so this was **not built or run on Windows**.\n\n**Not blocking:** if attach succeeds but the `CONOUT$` open fails (`:95-97`), `CONSOLE_ATTACHED` is already true, so the log goes nowhere and no box is shown.\n\n**Windows hand check:**\n- double-click;\n- a launch from cmd, PowerShell and Git Bash;\n- `> log.txt 2>&1` and a pipe;\n- a forced start-up failure;\n- a bad STEP import by double-click (no box should appear).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
